{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And your fear.</b> Of the doubled stems, from the form \"תִּרְאוּ חִתָּת\" (Job 6:21), like חִתַּתְכֶם." "<b>That the earth creeps.</b> The meaning is \"upon the earth,\" or הָאֲדָמָה may be the agent." "<b>Into your hand they are given.</b> For into your hand." "And some say that the bet of בְּכֹל is בְּכָל, and the vav of וּבְכָל is vav of the plural. But the near [meaning] is that it is joined with וּמוֹרַאֲכֶם."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {3 "The passage is textually difficult; rendered hyper-literally. The argument about individual letters (bet, vav) in surrounding words is cryptic and the reading of the witnesses may vary."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:43:53.677114022Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}